    description: "Lead (not investigated): four tests that read the whole source tree as text cost about 815 serial seconds per full run, 56% of what all 69 whole-tree text readers cost (1450 s of the suite's 23,084 s; timings from test_timings.json, reader set from the WI-zajuv measurement in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/text_reader_measurement_11102026/):\n\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_meta_write_discipline.py  226 s\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_catalogue_error_exit_code.py  212 s\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_id_floor_gate.py  199 s\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_producer_coherence.py  179 s\n\nA lint-like check over ~400 files should not need minutes. Hypotheses to check, none verified: the tree is rescanned per test case rather than once per module; a subprocess is spawned per file or per case; a full hypergumbo run on the repo is repeated. A fix here speeds every run that selects them, local and CI.\n\nFirst step: profile where the time goes in each (per-test durations, then a profiler on the slowest case). Done when each of the four is either faster with the numbers recorded, or has a stated reason its cost is necessary."  # 9e02
